11.0.0 — the earlier instrument's look: chosen is off-white, green is a signal; the plug-ins play in full and fit a phone-high window

What is new since 10068. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds; the render-event
and unit-format rules have tests of their own, and nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Look: a chosen view, a switched-on button (Mute, Solo, Loop, Click, Keys, an effect that is on)
  and a page's main action (the number pad's OK) are an off-white tile with a black label. The
  green is kept for what sounds or is measured: Play shows a green glyph while the song plays,
  and so does a track's stop button while its clip plays. Recording stays red.
- Buttons: a button that is not lit has a visible outline (it had a divider's hairline).
- Keys: the key strip stands under Instrument, Tracks, Arrange and Session; Mixer, Field and Sky
  keep their whole height. The Keys switch is unchanged.
- Audio Units in other apps: the instruments are not demo-locked while the purchase is not on
  sale — no pause, no demo sentence; "Echoelmusic Plugins…" offers nothing to buy or restore.
- Plug-in window: every control is in one grid; a named choice (Engine, Waveform, Filter) opens
  a menu; rows only one engine plays show while that engine is chosen; in a window under 340
  points high the title goes.
- Audio Units, in a host: numbers a host sends that are no time or no address can no longer
  stop the units; an instrument says it is stereo with no input and refuses another format
  when the host sets it; a host's reset silences the instrument.
- Plugins from other makers: music effects are offered under Add Effect; an export tells its
  units that it renders offline; a plugin that is installed but did not start is no longer
  called "not installed".
- Go Live: the streaming library is HaishinKit 2.3.0 (it was 2.2.5).

Previous: 11.0.0 (10068) — one name, Echoelmusic; a stream and a take finish stopping before
the next begins; 10067 — warp modes, a playhead you can move, zoom and waveforms.
Earlier: git history.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (answer each yes or no):
1. AUM: load "Echoelmusic: Synth" and hold a note for 40 seconds: does it sound without a
   pause, and is there no demo sentence in its window?
2. AUM on the iPhone, Synth window at its usual size: are Engine, Waveform, Filter, Cutoff and
   Resonance on screen without scrolling, and does tapping Engine open a list with all eleven
   names?
3. In the app: are the chosen view and a Mute or Solo that is on off-white with black letters,
   and does Play show a green glyph while the song plays — and can you tell at a glance what
   is on?
4. Open Mixer, Field and Sky: is the key strip gone there, and is it back under Instrument and
   Tracks?
5. Go Live to a destination, wait for the On Air clock, press Stop Stream: does the stream
   arrive at the destination and stop cleanly?
